---
// /devshop/demo/illustrative — a fully hand-built, static sample solution
// document. Exists because the real generation pipeline
// (classifyAndBuild -> Claude) is temporarily paused for lack of API
// credit — see GENERATION_PAUSED in devshop.astro. Shown after the
// #illustrative-notice disclosure screen, never linked to directly as if
// it were a real client's document. Delete once live generation is back
// and the disclosure screen is removed.
import { site } from '../../../data/site';

const whatsappNumber = '919999277240'; // WhatsApp only — click-to-chat link below.
const whatsappHref = `https://wa.me/${whatsappNumber}?text=${encodeURIComponent("Hi — I just ran the DevShop sample decision analysis and want to talk about my own problem.")}`;

const title = 'Sample solution document — Fast Tech Dev Shop';
const description =
  'A full, real example of what a DevShop solution document looks like: a common finance-ops problem, a proven framework applied, and an interactive mechanism with real AI agents running end to end.';
const canonical = new URL('/devshop/demo/illustrative', site.domain).href;
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
  <title>{title}</title>
  <meta name="description" content={description} />
  <link rel="canonical" href={canonical} />
  <meta name="robots" content="noindex, follow" />
  <link rel="icon" href="/devshop-favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml" />

  <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
  <meta property="og:site_name" content="DevShop" />
  <meta property="og:title" content={title} />
  <meta property="og:description" content={description} />
  <meta property="og:url" content={canonical} />
  <meta property="og:image" content={new URL('/devshop-og.png', site.domain).href} />
  <meta property="og:image:width" content="1200" />
  <meta property="og:image:height" content="630" />
  <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image" />
  <meta name="twitter:title" content={title} />
  <meta name="twitter:description" content={description} />
  <meta name="twitter:image" content={new URL('/devshop-og.png', site.domain).href} />

  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
  <link
    href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Newsreader:ital,opsz,wght@0,6..72,500;0,6..72,600;1,6..72,500&family=Archivo:wght@400;500;600&family=IBM+Plex+Mono:wght@400;500&display=swap"
    rel="stylesheet"
  />
</head>
<body>
  <div class="illus-banner">
    <span>A real example, not your problem yet — <a href="/devshop">bring us yours →</a></span>
  </div>

  <main class="brief">
    <div class="doc-header">
      <div class="eyebrow">SOLUTION BRIEF</div>
      <h1>What we heard, and what we're proposing.</h1>
      <div class="doc-meta">
        <div class="doc-meta-row"><span class="doc-meta-label">Prepared for</span>Meridian Supply Co — Finance / AR</div>
        <div class="doc-meta-row"><span class="doc-meta-label">Date</span>Illustrative example</div>
        <div class="doc-meta-row"><span class="doc-meta-label">Status</span>Sample only — shown while live generation is paused</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="illus-picked-note">We picked this one on purpose: it's not the hardest problem we solve, it's the <strong>most common</strong> — a pattern we see across most businesses that take in payments against invoices. The mechanism below is the same standard solution we'd build for almost any business with this pattern, tuned to your real numbers and your real tools.</p>

    <blockquote class="submitted-problem">
      <span class="submitted-label">What you told us</span>
      "Our AR team manually logs every incoming customer invoice payment against open invoices, and we keep finding mismatches weeks later when the books don't reconcile."
    </blockquote>

    <section class="block">
      <div class="section-head"><span class="section-num">§01</span><h2>The problem</h2></div>
      <div class="card">
        <p class="card-title">There's no automated match step between the bank feed and open invoices — every payment gets eyeballed by hand, whether it's a clean match or a genuine exception. The team isn't slow; the process makes no distinction between the two.</p>
        <p class="card-function"><span class="card-tag">Business function</span>Finance / Accounts Receivable</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="block framework-block">
      <div class="section-head"><span class="section-num">§02</span><h2>Grounded in a proven approach</h2></div>
      <div class="card">
        <p class="card-title"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/DMAIC" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Six Sigma — DMAIC</a></p>
        <p class="card-function">Define, Measure, Analyze, Improve, Control</p>
        <p class="plain-copy">The standard method for fixing a broken process without guessing — measure what's actually happening today, find the specific step causing the failure, fix that step, then control it so it doesn't drift back. Not reinvented per client; applied the same way every time this pattern shows up.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="block">
      <div class="section-head"><span class="section-num">§03</span><h2>How we'd apply it</h2></div>
      <div class="card">
        <p class="card-title">Automated payment-to-invoice matching, with real AI agents doing the work</p>
        <p class="plain-copy">Four agents, each with one job: <strong>Data Extraction</strong> reads the payment off the bank feed, <strong>Reconciliation/Matching</strong> checks it against open invoices, <strong>Exception/Diagnosis</strong> flags anything that doesn't clear automatically, and <strong>Notification</strong> routes the real exceptions to a person. Press Run below to watch one actual payment move through it.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="walkthrough-intro">
      <p class="walkthrough-eyebrow">See it work</p>
      <h2 class="walkthrough-heading">The interactive walkthrough</h2>
      <p class="artefact-caption">One real payment, run through the actual mechanism — press <strong>Run</strong> in the "See it run" tab.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="browser-chrome">
      <div class="browser-chrome-bar">
        <span class="chrome-dot chrome-dot--red"></span>
        <span class="chrome-dot chrome-dot--yellow"></span>
        <span class="chrome-dot chrome-dot--green"></span>
        <div class="chrome-address">
          <svg width="13" height="13" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M6 10V8a6 6 0 1112 0v2M5 10h14a1 1 0 011 1v9a1 1 0 01-1 1H5a1 1 0 01-1-1v-9a1 1 0 011-1z" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
          </svg>
          <span class="chrome-address-text">app.meridiansupply.co</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="artefact-embed">
        <div class="kt-tabs" id="ktTabs">
          <button type="button" class="kt-tab active" data-kttab="decision">The problem</button>
          <button type="button" class="kt-tab" data-kttab="connects">How it connects</button>
          <button type="button" class="kt-tab" data-kttab="run">See it run</button>
          <button type="button" class="kt-tab" data-kttab="impact">Business impact</button>
        </div>

        <div class="kt-panel active" data-ktpanel="decision">
          <p class="kt-panel-intro">A common problem, not a rare one: incoming payments arrive faster than anyone can match them by hand, so the whole batch gets touched by a human — even the ones that are a clean, obvious match.</p>
          <div class="kt-stat-row">
            <div class="kt-stat-card"><div class="kt-stat-k">Root cause</div><div class="kt-stat-v">No automated match step between bank feed and open invoices</div></div>
            <div class="kt-stat-card"><div class="kt-stat-k">Owner</div><div class="kt-stat-v">Accounts Receivable</div></div>
            <div class="kt-stat-card"><div class="kt-stat-k">P&amp;L line</div><div class="kt-stat-v">AR labor cost</div></div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="kt-panel" data-ktpanel="connects">
          <div class="kt-flow">
            <div class="kt-flow-node">Accounting system (bank feed)</div>
            <span class="kt-flow-arrow">→</span>
            <div class="kt-flow-node">Reconciliation mechanism</div>
            <span class="kt-flow-arrow">→</span>
            <div class="kt-flow-node">Email — AR Lead</div>
          </div>
          <p class="kt-agents-title">Agents involved</p>
          <div class="kt-agent-chips">
            <span class="kt-agent-chip">Data Extraction Agent</span>
            <span class="kt-agent-chip">Reconciliation/Matching Agent</span>
            <span class="kt-agent-chip">Exception/Diagnosis Agent</span>
            <span class="kt-agent-chip">Notification Agent</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="kt-panel" data-ktpanel="run">
          <div class="kt-run-controls">
            <button class="kt-run" id="ktRun">▶ Run the mechanism</button>
            <span class="kt-run-status" id="ktRunStatus">Payment #PMT-88213 · ₹1,84,500 · Orbis Retail</span>
          </div>
          <div class="kt-run-grid">
            <div class="kt-scenario">
              <div class="kt-sc-step" data-step="1">
                <div class="kt-sc-num">1</div>
                <div>
                  <div class="kt-sc-label">Data in</div>
                  <div class="kt-sc-body">Payment record pulled from the accounting system's bank feed.</div>
                  <div class="kt-record" id="ktRec1">
                    <div class="kt-record-row"><span>Payment ID</span><span>PMT-88213</span></div>
                    <div class="kt-record-row"><span>Amount</span><span>₹1,84,500</span></div>
                    <div class="kt-record-row"><span>Payer</span><span>Orbis Retail Pvt Ltd</span></div>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="kt-sc-step" data-step="2">
                <div class="kt-sc-num">2</div>
                <div>
                  <div class="kt-sc-label">Processing — DMAIC Measure/Analyze</div>
                  <div class="kt-sc-body">Checked against 14 open invoices. No single invoice matches ₹1,84,500 exactly.</div>
                  <div class="kt-record" id="ktRec2">
                    <div class="kt-record-row"><span>Candidate match</span><span>INV-4471 + INV-4483</span></div>
                    <div class="kt-record-row"><span>Variance</span><span>−₹120 (bank charge)</span></div>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="kt-sc-step" data-step="3">
                <div class="kt-sc-num">3</div>
                <div>
                  <div class="kt-sc-label">Outcome — escalated</div>
                  <div class="kt-sc-body">A ₹120 variance is outside auto-approve tolerance — routed to the AR Lead.</div>
                  <div class="kt-esc-card" id="ktEsc">
                    <div class="kt-esc-subject">Payment #PMT-88213 needs review — multi-invoice match, ₹120 short</div>
                    <div class="kt-esc-action">Action needed: approve match, write off ₹120</div>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="kt-agent-pane">
              <div class="kt-agent-pane-title">Agent activity</div>
              <div class="kt-agent-log" id="ktAgentLog">
                <div class="kt-agent-line show"><span class="kt-who">Data Extraction Agent</span> — idle</div>
                <div class="kt-agent-line show"><span class="kt-who">Reconciliation/Matching Agent</span> — idle</div>
                <div class="kt-agent-line show"><span class="kt-who">Exception/Diagnosis Agent</span> — idle</div>
                <div class="kt-agent-line show"><span class="kt-who">Notification Agent</span> — idle</div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="kt-result" id="ktResult" hidden>
            <a href="/devshop" class="kt-start">Start now &rarr;</a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="kt-panel" data-ktpanel="impact">
          <p class="kt-panel-intro">Same mechanism, run across every payment that month — not a one-off.</p>
          <div class="kt-impact-grid">
            <div class="kt-impact-card"><p class="kt-impact-num">40&rarr;8</p><p class="kt-impact-cap">hrs/month of manual matching, current vs. after</p></div>
            <div class="kt-impact-card"><p class="kt-impact-num">84%</p><p class="kt-impact-cap">of payments auto-matched, no human touch</p></div>
            <div class="kt-impact-card"><p class="kt-impact-num">32</p><p class="kt-impact-cap">AR hours recovered per month, without adding headcount</p></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <section class="block">
      <div class="section-head"><span class="section-num">§04</span><h2>Investment</h2></div>
      <div class="pricing-grid">
        <div class="pricing-card"><p class="pricing-amount">₹1,50,000</p><p class="pricing-label">First module — standard build</p></div>
        <div class="pricing-card"><p class="pricing-amount">₹75,000</p><p class="pricing-label">Each additional module, within 30 days of the first</p></div>
        <div class="pricing-card"><p class="pricing-amount">From ₹50,000<span class="pricing-per">/mo</span></p><p class="pricing-label">DevShop Care + Optimisation, per live module</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="payment-terms">
        <h3 class="payment-terms-label">Payment terms</h3>
        <div class="payment-terms-grid">
          <div class="payment-terms-item"><span class="payment-terms-pct">25%</span><span class="payment-terms-when">On confirmation — secures your build slot, starts the 30-day clock</span></div>
          <div class="payment-terms-item"><span class="payment-terms-pct">50%</span><span class="payment-terms-when">At the shadow run (Day 26) — once it's built and running against your real data</span></div>
          <div class="payment-terms-item"><span class="payment-terms-pct">25%</span><span class="payment-terms-when">On go-live (Day 30) — once the full run is live and handed over</span></div>
        </div>
        <p class="payment-terms-note"><strong>Ongoing:</strong> DevShop Care + Optimisation is billed monthly in advance — the first payment is due at the end of month 1, covering month 2, not on a delay.</p>
      </div>
      <p class="ptm-forward-note">A full PTM<sup>&trade;</sup> (Process, Training, Mapping) operating-model breakdown — task-by-task, human vs. AI — ships as part of implementation, not before. <a href="/devshop/demo/ptm-sample">See a sample PTM document →</a></p>
    </section>

    <div class="appendix-section">
      <h3>Why we picked this one</h3>
      <ul class="bullets flat">
        <li><span class="bullet-label">Common, not hard</span>Payment reconciliation is one of the highest-frequency finance-ops problems we see — not a showcase edge case, the exact pattern most businesses taking payments against invoices already have.</li>
        <li><span class="bullet-label">Standard solution</span>Same four-agent mechanism every time this pattern shows up. What changes per client is the numbers and the tools, not the approach.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="appendix-section">
      <h3>The honest objections</h3>
      <ul class="bullets flat">
        <li><span class="bullet-label">"Isn't this just AI hype?"</span>The agents aren't doing anything a human couldn't — they're doing it on every payment, instantly, and only escalating the ones that actually need judgement.</li>
        <li><span class="bullet-label">"What about the exceptions it gets wrong?"</span>It doesn't guess on exceptions — it escalates them, with the discrepancy already diagnosed, to a named person.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="cta-block">
      <p class="cta-line">This is exactly what your own solution document would look like — built around your actual problem, not this sample one.</p>
      <a href="/devshop" class="cta-btn cta-btn--primary">Start now &rarr;</a>

      <div class="talk-now">
        <p class="talk-now-line">Or, if you'd rather just talk it through first —</p>
        <div class="talk-now-links">
          <a href={whatsappHref} target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="talk-now-link talk-now-link--whatsapp">
            <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12.04 2C6.58 2 2.13 6.45 2.13 11.91c0 1.75.46 3.46 1.32 4.96L2.05 22l5.25-1.38c1.44.79 3.06 1.2 4.71 1.2h.004c5.46 0 9.91-4.45 9.91-9.91 0-2.65-1.03-5.14-2.9-7.01A9.85 9.85 0 0012.04 2zm5.79 14.11c-.24.68-1.4 1.3-1.93 1.38-.49.08-1.11.11-1.79-.11-.41-.13-.94-.3-1.62-.59-2.85-1.23-4.71-4.1-4.85-4.29-.14-.19-1.16-1.54-1.16-2.94 0-1.4.73-2.08.99-2.37.26-.28.57-.35.76-.35.19 0 .38 0 .54.01.18.01.41-.07.64.49.24.57.81 1.98.88 2.13.07.14.12.31.02.5-.09.19-.14.31-.28.47-.14.16-.29.36-.42.48-.14.14-.28.28-.12.55.16.28.71 1.17 1.53 1.9 1.05.94 1.94 1.23 2.21 1.37.28.14.44.12.6-.07.16-.19.68-.79.87-1.06.19-.28.37-.23.63-.14.26.09 1.66.78 1.94.93.28.14.47.21.54.33.07.12.07.68-.17 1.36z"/></svg>
            WhatsApp {whatsappNumber.replace(/^91/, '+91 ')}
          </a>
          <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`} class="talk-now-link">{site.email}</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="footer-bar"><span class="footer-bar-text">Built fast, <em>for real businesses</em><sup>TM</sup></span></div>
  </main>
</body>
</html>

<style>
  :root {
    color-scheme: light;
    --ink: #1c1f22; --ink-soft: #4a4f54; --muted: #767c82; --hair: rgba(28,31,34,0.13);
    --paper: #f4f2ec; --gold: #7d6435; --gold-soft: #eee7d6; --blue: #4d7a94;
  }
  *, *::before, *::after { box-sizing: border-box; }
  html, body { margin: 0; background: var(--paper); width: 100%; overflow-x: hidden; }
  body { font-family: 'Archivo', system-ui, sans-serif; color: #2a2f3a; }
  a { color: inherit; }

  .illus-banner {
    background: #2a2f3a; color: #f4f2ec; text-align: center; padding: 12px 20px;
    font-size: 13px; letter-spacing: 0.02em; position: sticky; top: 0; z-index: 10;
  }
  .illus-banner a { color: #d4af37; font-weight: 600; text-decoration: none; }
  .illus-banner a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }

  .brief { max-width: 760px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 48px 40px 40px; }
  .eyebrow { font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 0.16em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--gold); font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 16px; }

  .doc-header { padding-bottom: 28px; margin-bottom: 32px; border-bottom: 3px double var(--hair); }
  h1 { font-family: 'Newsreader', Georgia, serif; font-weight: 600; font-size: clamp(28px, 4vw, 38px); line-height: 1.2; margin: 0 0 24px; max-width: 22ch; color: var(--ink); }
  .doc-meta { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 24px 32px; }
  .doc-meta-row { font-size: 13px; color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .doc-meta-label { display: block; font-size: 10.5px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.06em; color: var(--muted); margin-bottom: 3px; }

  .illus-picked-note { font-size: 13.5px; color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.6; margin: 0 0 24px; max-width: 62ch; }
  .illus-picked-note strong { color: var(--ink); }

  .submitted-problem {
    margin: 0 0 40px; padding: 16px 20px; border-left: 3px solid var(--gold);
    background: var(--gold-soft); font-style: italic; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.6; color: #4a453e;
  }
  .submitted-label {
    display: block; font-style: normal; font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--gold); margin-bottom: 4px;
  }

  .section-head { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 12px; margin: 0 0 16px; padding-bottom: 10px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hair); }
  .section-num { font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 500; color: var(--gold); letter-spacing: 0.02em; }
  h2 { font-family: 'Newsreader', Georgia, serif; font-weight: 600; font-size: 19px; margin: 0; color: var(--ink); }
  .block { margin-bottom: 36px; }
  .card { padding: 0; }
  .card-title { font-size: 16px; font-weight: 500; line-height: 1.5; margin: 0 0 10px; color: var(--ink); }
  .card-function { font-size: 13px; color: var(--muted); margin: 0 0 10px; }
  .card-tag { display: inline-block; font-size: 10.5px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.05em; color: var(--gold); border: 1px solid var(--gold); border-radius: 3px; padding: 2px 7px; margin-right: 8px; }
  .plain-copy { font-size: 14.5px; line-height: 1.65; color: var(--ink-soft); margin: 0; }

  .walkthrough-intro { max-width: 640px; margin: 48px auto 28px; text-align: center; }
  .walkthrough-eyebrow { font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 0.16em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--gold); font-weight: 600; margin: 0 0 8px; }
  .walkthrough-heading { font-family: 'Newsreader', Georgia, serif; font-weight: 600; font-size: clamp(24px, 3.4vw, 32px); color: var(--ink); margin: 0 0 10px; }
  .artefact-caption { font-size: 14.5px; color: var(--ink-soft); margin: 0; }
  .artefact-caption strong { color: var(--gold); }

  .browser-chrome {
    width: min(1180px, calc(100% - 0px)); margin: 0 auto 56px;
    border-radius: 14px; overflow: hidden; background: #e8e6e0;
    border: 2px solid var(--gold); box-shadow: 0 32px 72px -24px rgba(26,36,56,0.35), 0 0 0 6px var(--gold-soft);
  }
  .browser-chrome-bar { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; padding: 14px 18px; background: #ecebe6; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(36,33,29,0.1); }
  .chrome-dot { width: 13px; height: 13px; border-radius: 50%; display: inline-block; flex: none; }
  .chrome-dot--red { background: #ec6a5e; }
  .chrome-dot--yellow { background: #f4bf4f; }
  .chrome-dot--green { background: #61c454; }
  .chrome-address {
    flex: 1; margin-left: 14px; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px;
    background: #fbfaf8; border: 1px solid rgba(36,33,29,0.1); border-radius: 7px;
    padding: 7px 16px; font-size: 13.5px; color: #6b6459; max-width: 420px;
  }
  .chrome-address svg { color: #8a8378; flex: none; }
  .chrome-address-text { overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis; white-space: nowrap; }
  .artefact-embed { background: #fff; padding: 28px 32px 36px; }

  .kt-tabs { display: flex; gap: 2px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hair); margin-bottom: 24px; }
  .kt-tab {
    font-family: 'Archivo', sans-serif; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--muted);
    background: none; border: none; cursor: pointer; padding: 10px 2px; margin-right: 24px;
    border-bottom: 2.5px solid transparent; transition: color 0.15s, border-color 0.15s; position: relative; top: 1px;
  }
  .kt-tab:hover { color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .kt-tab.active { color: var(--gold); border-bottom-color: var(--gold); }
  .kt-panel { display: none; }
  .kt-panel.active { display: block; animation: kt-fade 0.25s ease; }
  @keyframes kt-fade { from { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(4px); } to { opacity: 1; transform: translateY(0); } }

  .kt-panel-intro { font-size: 14px; color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.6; margin: 0 0 20px; max-width: 60ch; }
  .kt-panel-intro em { font-style: italic; color: var(--ink); }
  .kt-panel-cta { font-size: 13px; color: var(--muted); margin: 20px 0 0; }
  .kt-panel-cta strong { color: var(--gold); }

  .kt-criteria-static { display: flex; flex-direction: column; }
  .kt-static-row {
    display: flex; justify-content: space-between; padding: 11px 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--hair);
    font-size: 13.5px; color: var(--ink);
  }
